## Starting point

The project starts as a playable browser voxel action-adventure with a blocky pixel-art look; replace or extend it as the game takes shape.

- **Demo level "Meadow Crossing"** (`src/content/demo.js`, level id `meadow-v1`): a deterministic finite meadow with a river, bridge, small jump route, one training guardian, three crystals, a healing checkpoint and an exit beacon. Collecting all crystals and defeating the guardian unlocks the beacon; exploration and building continue after completion.
- **Mechanics:** third-person movement with physics (jump, sprint, crouch, swim, climb, step-up), melee combat with reach, facing, cooldown and knockback, mining and placing blocks with lighting and mesh updates; spawn and objective cells are protected and placement cannot overlap the player.
- **Saves and settings:** checkpoint, objectives and up to 2048 edited cells persist in this browser per `APP_SLUG`; loading restarts at the checkpoint with full health. Graphics quality, volume, look sensitivity, inverted look, field of view and camera shake persist too.
- **Interface:** keyboard and mouse (pointer lock) and standard gamepads; menus for continue, new game (with confirmation), settings, pause, completion and errors. Losing focus or pointer lock pauses the game; graphics and storage failures are shown.
- **Presentation:** all textures, skins and sounds are generated procedurally. There is no backend, account, multiplayer or cloud save.

